{"name":"Oceanside","hex":"#015a6b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Oceanside","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in San Diego County, California, United States.","A hamlet and census-designated place in the town of Hempstead, Nassau County, New York, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Oceanside"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oceanside, California","blocks":[{"text":"Oceanside is a beach city in the North County area of San Diego County, California, United States. The city had a population of 174,068 at the 2020 United States census, making it the most populous city in the North County region of San Diego. The city is a popular tourist destination, owing to its historic landmarks, beaches, and architecture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Oceanside_SW01_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Oceanside_SW01_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oceanside%2C_California","wikidata":"Q488924"},{"title":"Oceanside Transit Center","blocks":[{"text":"Oceanside Transit Center is a major railway interchange in Oceanside, California, serving both intercity and suburban/commuter services. The station is used by Amtrak on the route of its Pacific Surfliner service between San Diego and San Luis Obispo. It is also a terminus for two different regional transit operators – Metrolink, the commuter rail operator for the Los Angeles area, has two of its services, the Orange County Line and Inland Empire–Orange County Line, that terminate at Oceanside, while the North County Transit District (NCTD), the operator for most of the public transport in the North County, has its COASTER and SPRINTER services also terminating at Oceanside. Oceanside Transit Center is also served by Greyhound Lines and numerous NCTD BREEZE buses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/A_COASTER_train_at_Oceanside_Transit_Center_in_March_2024.jpg/330px-A_COASTER_train_at_Oceanside_Transit_Center_in_March_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oceanside_Transit_Center","wikidata":"Q3095815"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Oceanside%2C_CA_USA_-_Mission_San_Luis_Rey_De_Francia%2C_1798_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Oceanside%2C_CA_USA_-_Mission_San_Luis_Rey_De_Francia%2C_1798_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Oceanside%2C_CA_USA_-_Mission_San_Luis_Rey_De_Francia%2C_1798_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Oceanside%2C_CA_USA_-_Mission_San_Luis_Rey_De_Francia%2C_1798_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Oceanside%2C_CA_USA_-_Mission_San_Luis_Rey_De_Francia%2C_1798_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Oceanside%2C_CA_USA_-_Mission_San_Luis_Rey_De_Francia%2C_1798_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOceanside%2C_CA_USA_-_Mission_San_Luis_Rey_De_Francia%2C_1798_-_panoramio_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Oceanside_Civic_Center-9.jpg/500px-Oceanside_Civic_Center-9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Oceanside_Civic_Center-9.jpg/1280px-Oceanside_Civic_Center-9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Oceanside_Civic_Center-9.jpg/500px-Oceanside_Civic_Center-9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai